============================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
============================================================

1.  Python virtual environment creation fails: Install the matching venv
    package: apt-get update apt-get install -y python3.12-venv If using
    another Python version, install its matching venv package.

2.  docker: command not found: The current Killercoda scenario may not
    provide Docker. Do not continue with Docker commands unless Docker
    is available.

3.  Jenkins browser says localhost refused: Do not use laptop localhost.
    Expose Killercoda port 8080 and open the generated Killercoda URL.

4.  Jenkins cannot find set3: Confirm set3/ is committed and pushed to
    the main branch.

5.  Jenkins cannot find requirements.txt: Confirm set3/requirements.txt
    is committed and pushed.

6.  Git says “Author identity unknown”: Configure Git once: git config
    –global user.name “YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME” git config –global
    user.email “YOUR_GITHUB_EMAIL”

7.  Git push asks for authentication: Authenticate using an authorized
    GitHub credential or token. Never paste a password or token into a
    public file or practical README.

8.  Git says “nothing to commit”: Run: git status The files may already
    be committed. Verify them on GitHub.

9.  GitHub Actions fails: Open Actions, select the failed run, open the
    test job, and inspect the first failed step. Confirm
    set3/requirements.txt, set3/app.py, and set3/test_app.py exist in
    the repository.

